    "q-215884": {
      "dom_id": "step-q215884",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence ${a}_{n}$ is defined by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+15,\\,{a}_{1}=0,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$\n\nThe $6$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=0,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $6$th term ${a}_{6}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+15=0+15=15 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+15=15+15=30 \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+15=30+15=45 \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{4}+15=45+15=60 \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{5}+15=60+15=75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=75.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
